2. 3.</NOTE>  adfinitate
 <COL N="0045B"></COL> sibi coniunxerat. Filiorum ac filiarum tantam
 <NOTE N="20" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> tantum 1. 2. 5. B 1—5.</NOTE>  in educando curam habuit, ut nunquam domi
positus sine ipsis caenaret <NOTE N="c" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045C"></COL> Cf. ibid., c. 64.</NOTE>  numquam iter sine illis
ageret <NOTE N="21" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> faceret 3 b. 4. 5. 8 b. 10. 10 c. 11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gemblac.</HI>  faciebat B 1—5.</NOTE> : adequitabant <NOTE N="22" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> adequibant,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  adequitabant 1.</NOTE>  ei filii, filiae vero pene <NOTE N="23" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> paene B 1. pene B 3. 3 d. 4 b. penes 6 b. B 2. 5. paulo 10 c.</NOTE>  sequebantur,
quarum agmen extremum ex satellitum
numero ad hoc ordinati tuebantur. Quae cum pulcherrimae
essent et ab eo plurimum diligerentur,
mirum dictu <NOTE N="24" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  8 b.</NOTE> , quod nullam earum <NOTE N="25" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> eorum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  earum 1.</NOTE>  cuiquam
aut suorum aut exterorum nuptum dare voluit; sed
omnes secum usque ad obitum suum in domo <NOTE N="26" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> domu,  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  domo 1.</NOTE>  sua
retinuit <NOTE N="27" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> retenuit 4. 5.</NOTE> , dicens, se earum contubernio carere non
posse. Ac propter hoc, licet alias felix, adversae fortunae
malignitatem expertus est; quod tamen ita
dissimulavit, ac si de eis nulla umquam alicuius
probri suspicio exorta, vel fama dispersa fuisset <NOTE N="28" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  8 b. 4 b.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="d" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045C"></COL> Hruothrudem Hludowicum abbatem S. Dionysii,
Bertham Angilberto filios genuisse, constat.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0045"><COL N="0045C"></COL> 20. Erat ei filius nomine Pippinus <NOTE N="29" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> pipinus 11. B 2. 3. 3
b.</NOTE> , ex concubina <NOTE N="e" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0046" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0046C"></COL> Himiltrude, Ann. Lauriss. min. T. I, p. 119, 2.
Pro legitima eam habuisse videtur Stephanus III papa,
in epistola 45 codicis Carolini.</NOTE> 
editus, cuius inter caeteros facere mentionem <NOTE N="30" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> m. f. 3 b. 4. 5. 7 a. 9. 10. 10 b. 11 c. B 1—5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">certeet alii.</HI>  mentionem nullam fecimus 8 b.</NOTE> 
distuli; facie quidem pulcher, sed gibbo <NOTE N="31" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> gigbo 3 c.
gypbo B 1. gyppo 10. 10 b. c. B 2. 3. 3 c. 3 d. 4. 4 b. gippo B 3 b. gybbo B 5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ex corr.</HI>  3 c.</NOTE>  deformis.
 <COL N="0046A"></COL> Is <NOTE N="32" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> His B 2.</NOTE>  cum pater, bello <NOTE N="33" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> bellum.
suscepit 1.</NOTE>  contra Hunos <NOTE N="34" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> hunnos 2 c. 11 d.</NOTE>  suscepto, in
Baioaria hyemaret <NOTE N="35" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> hymaret 2 <HI REND="ITALIC">a m. corr.</HI>  hyemaret 1. hiemaret 3 b. 4. 10. 10 b. c. 11. B 1—5.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">et alii.</HI></NOTE> , aegritudine simulata, cum quibusdam
e primoribus Francorum, qui <NOTE N="36" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> qui sibi . . illuserant 8 b.  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3.</NOTE>  eum vana
regni promissione inlexerant, adversus patrem coniuravit.
Quem post fraudem detectam et dampnationem
coniuratorum <NOTE N="37" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> cenubii B 1. 2.</NOTE>  detonsum in coenobio <NOTE N="38" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> priuma 11.</NOTE>  Prumia
religiosae vitae, iamque volentem, vacare permisit.
Facta est et alia prius contra eum in Germania valida
coniuratio, cuius auctores partim luminibus
orbati, partim membris incolumes <NOTE N="39" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> incolomes 4. B 1—5.</NOTE> , omnes tamen
exilio deportati sunt <NOTE N="40" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> in exilium acti sunt 8 b.</NOTE> ; neque ullus ex eis est interfectus,
nisi tres <NOTE N="41" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> III.  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  hi B 2. in B 2.</NOTE>  tantum qui, cum se, ne comprehenderentur,
strictis gladiis defenderent, aliquos
etiam occidissent, quia aliter coerceri non poterant,
interempti sunt. Harum tamen coniurationum Fastradae
 <COL N="0046B"></COL> <NOTE N="42" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> uastradae B 5.</NOTE>  reginae crudelitas causa et origo extitisse
creditur, et idcirco in ambabus <NOTE N="43" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> in a.  <HI REND="ITALIC">lineae superscriptum</HI> 
1.</NOTE>  contra regem
conspiratum est, quia uxoris crudelitati <NOTE N="44" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> crudelitate B 1. 2.</NOTE>  consentiens,
a suae naturae benignitate ac solita mansuetudine
immaniter <NOTE N="45" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest, 2a manu suppletum</HI>  1.</NOTE>  exorbitasse videbatur. Ceterum <NOTE N="46" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Sequentia in editis capiti 21 adiiciuntur.</HI></NOTE> 
per omne vitae suae tempus ita cum summo omnium
amore atque favore et domi et foris conversatus est,
ut nunquam ei vel minima iniustae crudelitatis nota
a quoquam fuisset obiecta.</P> <P COM="0046">21. Amabat <NOTE N="47" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> Amaibat 1.</NOTE>  peregrinos, et in eis suscipiendis <NOTE N="48" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> et eorum suscipiendorum 8 b.</NOTE> 
magnam habebat curam, adeo ut plerumque <NOTE N="49" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> plerumque 1. 5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest in reliquis.</HI></NOTE>  eorum
multitudo non solum palatio, verum etiam regno
non inmerito videretur onerosa. Ipse tamen prae <NOTE N="50" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> pro
8 b.</NOTE> 
magnitudine animi huiuscemodi pondere minime
gravabatur, cum etiam ingentia incommoda laude liberalitatis
 <COL N="0046C"></COL> ac bonae famae mercede compensaret.</P> <P COM="0046">22 <NOTE N="51" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">capp. 22—26 usque</HI>  qua ab infantia  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  5.</NOTE>  Corpore <NOTE N="f" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0046" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0046C"></COL> Cf. Suet. Tiber., c. 68; Aug. 79, Calig. 50.</NOTE>  fuit amplo <NOTE N="52" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3 c.</NOTE>  atque robusto <NOTE N="53" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0045" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0045"></COL> robusta st. B 1. 2.</NOTE> , statura
 <COL N="0047A"></COL> eminenti, quae tamen iustam non excederet—nam
septem suorum pedum proceritatem eius constat
habuisse mensuram <NOTE N="1" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047"></COL> figuram 8 b.</NOTE> —apice <NOTE N="2" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047"></COL> a. c. r.  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3 c.</NOTE>  capitis rotundo, oculis
praegrandibus ac vegetis, naso paululum <NOTE N="3" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047"></COL> paulolum B 1.</NOTE>  mediocritatem
 <NOTE N="4" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047"></COL> in mediocritatem 1. 2.</NOTE>  excedenti, canitie pulchra <NOTE N="a" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047C"></COL> Cf. Suet. Claud., c. 30.</NOTE> , facie laeta
et hilari. Unde formae auctoritas <NOTE N="b" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047C"></COL> Ibid.</NOTE>  ac dignitas tam
stanti quam sedenti plurima adquirebatur <NOTE N="5" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047"></COL> inerat 8 b.</NOTE> , quamquam
cervix obesa et brevior <NOTE N="c" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047C"></COL> Suet. Neron., c. 51.</NOTE> , venterque proiectior
 <NOTE N="d" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047C"></COL> Suet. Tit., c. 3.</NOTE>  videretur: tamen haec <NOTE N="6" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047"></COL> hoc
B 1. 3. 3 b.</NOTE>  caeterorum membrorum
celabat aequalitas <NOTE N="e" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047C"></COL> Cf. Suet. Aug., c. 79.</NOTE> . Incessu firmo, totaque
corporis habitudine virili, voce clara quidem, sed
quae minus corporis formae conveniret; valitudine
prospera <NOTE N="f" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047C"></COL> Cf. Suet. Claud., c. 31.</NOTE> , praeter quod, antequam decederet, per
quatuor <NOTE N="7" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047"></COL> quattuor B 1. 2.</NOTE>  annos crebro febribus <NOTE N="8" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047"></COL> febrius,  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  febribus 1.</NOTE>  corripiebatur, ad
extremum etiam uno pede claudicaret <NOTE N="9" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047"></COL> claudicarat 10. 10 b. c. claudicabat 11.
B 5. claudicavit 3 b.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="g" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047C"></COL> Cf. Suet. Aug., c. 80.</NOTE> . Et tunc
 <COL N="0047B"></COL> quidem plura suo arbitratu quam medicorum consilio
faciebat, quos pene exosos habebat, quod ei in
cibis assa, quibus assetus erat, dimittere, et elixis
adsuescere suadebant. Exercebatur assidue equitando
 <NOTE N="h" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047C"></COL> Suet. Tit., c. 3.</NOTE>  ac venando, quod illi <NOTE N="10" TYPE="Variantes Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0047" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0047"></COL> ei 1.</NOTE>  gentilicium erat: quia vix
